@@ -33,6 +33,8 @@ node bin/visual-merge.js <into-branch> <from-branch> --repo /path/to/your/repo -

 `<into-branch>` is the branch that gets modified — the one you would check out before merging. The CLI prints the merge it is computing to stderr before it starts, so a direction mistake is visible immediately. It never writes to the repository it inspects.

+It refuses rather than guesses. A branch name that does not resolve, a directory that is not a repository, git older than 2.38, or two branches with no shared history all exit non-zero with an explanation and write no JSON — `--allow-unrelated-histories` opts in to the last of those. A merge it computes but cannot fully explain is reported with an `unsupported[]` entry carrying git's own sentence, and the widget will not call such a merge cleanly merged.
+
 `npm run build` also generates `examples/basic.html`, which contains a real report from the fixture repository and the widget inlined. Open it by double-clicking; it needs no server.

 **The report contains your source code.** It is a static file like any other; a host that publishes it publishes the diff.
